  "summary_en": "European Parliament 2019 resolution setting out a comprehensive EU industrial policy for AI and robotics. It covers labour, research funding, data, cybersecurity, sectoral uses, liability, consumer protection, ethics-by-design, transparency and governance. It proposes a European AI regulatory agency and favours sectoral rules over a single comprehensive AI law.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Calls for consideration of a European regulatory agency for AI and algorithmic decision-making, with a risk assessment matrix and audits of algorithmic impact assessments",
   "Urges a single set of Union rules for autonomous vehicles and civilian drones to avoid a patchwork of national laws",
   "Calls for an ethical charter and ethics-by-design based on beneficence, non-maleficence, autonomy and justice",
   "Urges no EU funding for weaponised AI and a human-in-command approach for automated weapons",
   "Welcomes regulatory sandboxes and EU-wide standardisation, and calls for liability rules to be updated"
  ],
